@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Spaghetti Feed";
    bool isAdmin = User.HasClaim("isAdmin", "true");
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
}
<h2>Spaghetti Feed</h2>
<p>
    <h5>Hungry People Wanted!</h5>
    <blockquote>
        Every summer (typically on the Saturday closest to D-Day, 6 June), we hold our annual fund raisers: <em>The Spaghetti Feed</em>, which is an "All You Can Eat" spaghetti meal made fresh that day at our location by our members and served by our members.<br />
        Members of our league cook an original sauce and the spaghetti, and we serve the meals to our guests.
        <ul>
            <li>Tickets are typically $10 each and tickets are sold in advance (so we can anticipate how many are coming).</li>
            <li>Dine-in, for an All-You-Want experience or</li>
            <li>Take-out, with generous portions served.</li>
            <li>Bake Sale items are available, and are donated by many of our members' spouces.</li>
        </ul>
        Tickets are sold in advance. Some citizens buy tickets to show support, but never show. Tickets are also sold at the door.<br />
    </blockquote>
    <p>Our Patriot Sponsors donate $100 for the honor of having their business presented on the placemats that we set out for our guests. Most of these Patriot Sponsors
        choose to represent their interests with a business card, but coupons and discounts can also go in a spot. Multiple spots can also be purchased for Patriot Sponsors
        that want a larger presence on the placemats.</p>
    <center><img src="~/images/20260603Spaghetti.jpg" alt="Spaghetti Feed Placemat" style="width: 80%;" /></center>
</p>
